<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="498a5fc9-a384-52ca-8fd0-e0b66bcc8b9f" activityNameId="898bfba1-413c-5010-a316-566af458b38e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, tailings from hard coal milling, in impoundment</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, tailings from hard coal milling, in impoundment
na;
Synonyms: coal milling reject, coal washery refuse, coal refining discard, coal slurry; 
UUID: 95ff20e4-7e2c-4531-910e-d0d8eeb072c4
Waste-specific emissions from lignite spoil leachate. Short- and long-term emissions to groundwater from rainwater infiltration leaching. Leaching by lateral groundwater flow not included.; Geography: Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of coal tailings production in the world.
Location:  Data represents a worldwide average. Generic water infiltration rate according to weighted mean of major sites of coal tailings production in the world.
Technology: Mechanically stable and revegetated coal tailings impoundment
Time period: Average coal tailings composition from literature references. Transfer coefficients from prospective model, specific to coal tailings.
Production volume: Approx. 1167 Mio t/a coal tailings generation
Sampling: Disposal model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial tailings composition from various literature sources.  
Extrapolations: missing values adopted by proxy from lignite spoil
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from large literature survey. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions during a generic ecological planning horizon (60'000a). Maximal (upper boundary) long-term emissions represent the complete emissions of all landfilled material.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_95ff20e4-7e2c-4531-910e-d0d8eeb072c4.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
